00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:04.070 align:start position:0%
 
nowadays  most people have a smart watch to track  their fitness activities and also health  i've used so many different smart  watches over the years  and knowing my health status on a daily  basis has  helped me to stay on track with my  workouts diet  and also sleep the more data and  knowledge you have in regards to your  own body  the better you can manage your health so  after using so many different smart  watches  what should you look out for when it  comes to choosing the right watch to  monitor your health  what are the functions you need that's  what i'll be sharing  in this video  the first and most important element is  the battery life  i mean wouldn't you get annoyed if your  watch dies midday  or was halfway through your workout  because you've forgotten to charge it  well that has happened to me way too  many times before this  hence this really affects the accuracy  of tracking my health activities  since trying the huawei watch 3 i never  have to worry about this issue anymore  because  this watch can last up to 3 days in  smart mode  and 14 days in ultra long battery life  mode  this is the smart watch with the  strongest battery life  in the industry and good news guys the  huawei watch 3 will be launched in  malaysia  really soon  [Music]  as a fitness enthusiast i want a watch  that can offer me  all day health monitoring and that's  what this watch  does best the huawei watch 3 is based on  the new trusin  4.5 plus heart rate monitoring  technology  which intelligently monitors blood  oxygen saturation  24 7 and takes care of your blood oxygen  health around the clock  so why is it so important for you to  track your blood oxygen levels  when you're engaged in outdoor  activities at different altitudes  by monitoring your blood oxygen  saturation you can assess  your physical condition in real time and  adjust the intensity  of the current fitness the data can let  you understand how your body reacts  to the changing environment when you  work long hours without taking any  breaks  you'll need more oxygen to fill your  brain  however the human body can only take in  limited amount of oxygen  so as a result overworking can cause  dizziness  fatigue poor memory slow response and  even  serious damage to the brain so by  monitoring  your blood oxygen and sleep habits this  will help you to prioritize your health  and take the appropriate breaks when  necessary  if you look at the middle part of the  back of the case the corresponding  sensors are arranged  nearby so when the watch is worn and the  skin is close to the sensor  you can faintly see a red and green  light with huawei's  self-developed hardwood algorithm you  can understand  your heart rate in real time during  exercise  and guide you to exercise in a more  scientific way according to your fitness  goals  at the same time the watch 3 can also  monitor your stress state  in real time and provide breathing  suggestions  by practicing mindful breathing when you  are stressed out  this can help you to manage your  emotions and anxiety  this is a really useful feature for your  mental health  i wear this watch to sleep every night  to monitor my sleep patterns with the  huawei ai technology  it accurately identifies six typical  sleep problems  such as difficulty falling asleep light  sleep  easy waking at night multiple dreams  irregular work  and rest so by viewing the sleep report  you can know in detail  your rem sleep light sleep and deep  sleep  time ratios and intervals for example if  there is too little deep sleep the night  before  you can make adjustments by avoiding  high intensity physical activity  or reduce your caffeine intake closer to  bid time  one thing i really love about this watch  is that it supports more than  100 types of spots including common  spots such as running  spinning weight lifting heat and yoga  as well as niche spots such as  snowboarding  karate horse riding skateboarding and  more  so whatever spot you're into you'll be  able to track it with this watch  and check the exercise data on your  mobile phone so you can view your  exercise time  calories burned heart rate curve heart  rate interval  and more the watch 3 series also  supports  dual gps which provides more accurate  and precise routes for outdoor sports  finally because of the e-sim function  this watch also supports phone  monitoring and sos call for help  now this is an especially important  feature for your elderly parents who  live far away  or even for sports enthusiasts say in  the event that there is a fall detected  the sos function will be turned on and  it will enter into distress  mode the user will then have an option  to select emergency call  i felt but it's okay or i didn't fall  however in the event of an emergency you  can also trigger the  sos emergency help process by pressing  the up button  five times the e-sim can be purchased  through your local operators  in malaysia for me a good smart watch is  beyond recording simple health data  it can also provide the users with  better health management assistance  and that's what i really like about the  huawei watch 3.  it has great battery life provides real  all day health management  as well as detailed analysis reports and  recommendations  on your diet and exercise some of you  might be wondering  do i need to be a huawei mobile phone  user to use this watch  nope you can use this watch no matter  what phone you use  whether it's an iphone or other android  phone  so once you have your far away watch  simply scan the qr code  in the box and download the faraway  health app to connect  it is that simple so let me know in the  comments below how do you track your  health and fitness  and also what are the important features  you look out for  if you find this video to be useful then  do give this video a thumbs up  and share it on with your friends and  get them to start tracking their health  and fitness  don't forget to also hit the subscribe  button and check out a lot more fitness  videos on my youtube channel  all the best

